[gd_scene load_steps=9 format=3]

; A campfire. The stones are real kit art; the flame is a STAND-IN.
;
; The extracted subset has no campfire model, so this composes one from assets
; already in the ledger: eight `Pebble_Round_*` from the Quaternius Stylized
; Nature MegaKit laid in a 1.1m ring, three Kenney `log.glb` stacked in the
; middle. Those are the real thing at their authored scale. Only the flame
; itself is primitive geometry, because no pack in the repo has one.
;
; EVERYTHING THE FIRE DOES LIVES UNDER `Flame`: the two emissive cones and the
; light, together, so `Hearth.set_lit()` in scripts/building/station.gd turns
; the whole fire on and off with one visibility flag. An unlit campfire is
; visibly a cold ring of stones. If this node is renamed, rename it in
; `data/building/pieces.json` too — the definition names it there rather than
; the code hard-coding it.
;
; The light casts no shadows on purpose. A shadow-casting omni light is one of
; the most expensive things a scene can contain, and the player may build many
; of these; the sun already carries the scene's shadows.

